tmux with everything removed except tabs.
for running coding agents and ssh work.

     1 shell   2 codex   3 pi  [4 claude]      ^T new  ^W close  ^← ^→
    ╭─ Claude Code ─────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
    │                                                               │
    │                      Welcome back Yahya!                      │
    │                                                               │
    │                            ▐▛███▜▌                            │
    │                           ▝▜█████▛▘                           │
    │                             ▘▘ ▝▝                             │
    │                                                               │
    │                Opus 5 (1M context) with xhig…                 │
    │                          Claude Max                           │
    │                             ~/dev                             │
    │                                                               │
    ╰───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ❯ Try "how does <filepath> work?"
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      ⏵⏵ bypass permissions on (shift+tab to cycle) · ← for agents

no prefix key, no panes, no copy mode. chrome shortcuts:

    ctrl+T        new tab (pick claude / codex / pi / opencode / shell)
    ctrl+W        close tab
    ctrl+→ ←      next / previous tab

install:

    $ mkdir -p ~/.local/bin
    $ curl -o ~/.local/bin/tabs https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sueszli/tmux-tabs/master/tmux-tabs.sh
    $ chmod +x ~/.local/bin/tabs

usage:

    $ tabs

closing the terminal window leaves the agents running. `tabs` reattaches.
tabs close themselves when the agent exits. runs on its own tmux socket,
your ~/.tmux.conf is untouched. works in the stock macOS terminal and any
linux terminal, nothing to configure.

(chrome's ctrl+tab is impossible in a terminal: it's the same byte as tab.)
